# The bridge to "fluid_styled_content".
#
# Read by the site set "sbuerk/theme-extension-development-fsc" and by the
# static include registered from "Configuration/TCA/Overrides/sys_template.php"
# under the same path - the two delivery mechanisms the theme already has, see
# "docs/architecture/typoscript-delivery.md".
#
# --- What this is for -------------------------------------------------------
#
# The theme renders every classic content element itself and does not depend on
# "fluid_styled_content". Installed side by side, the two are not merely
# redundant, they are order dependent: that extension starts its own rendering
# with "lib.contentElement >" and rebuilds the object from nothing, so loaded
# after the theme it takes the theme's Fluid paths with it, and loaded before
# it leaves its own per-element data processing behind underneath the theme's.
# Neither outcome is anything an integrator chose.
#
# This file makes the combination defined: the classic branches are cleared and
# then declared again from the theme's own file, so the result is the rendering
# the theme produces on its own, whichever of the two extensions was loaded
# first.
#
# --- Why the branches are cleared rather than merged ------------------------
#
# "=<" and a plain assignment keep the children already on a path; only ">"
# removes them ("AbstractAstBuilder::handleIdentifierUnsetLine()"). Re-declaring
# "tt_content.textmedia" over the one "fluid_styled_content" left behind would
# therefore inherit whatever the theme does not happen to overwrite, key by
# key, and the leftovers are not cosmetic:
#
#   - "textmedia"/"textpic"/"image" keep that extension's "borderWidth" and
#     "borderPadding" on "GalleryProcessor", which the theme never sets;
#   - "table" is fed by "comma-separated-value" there and by this theme's own
#     "TableProcessor" here, and the two produce different shapes - a flat list
#     of rows against "{table.headerRow}"/"{table.bodyRows}"/"{table.footerRow}";
#   - "menu_categorized_content" is assigned to "content" there and to "items"
#     here, and its query is a join rather than the portable subquery this
#     theme uses;
#   - the nine "MenuProcessor" menus differ in "special", "levels" and sorting.
#
# A merged branch renders empty or wrong for each of those, and it does so
# silently. Clearing first is what makes the bridged rendering identical to the
# standalone rendering rather than approximately like it - which is exactly
# what "FluidStyledContentBridgeTest" asserts, byte for byte.
#
# --- Which branches, and which one is left alone ----------------------------
#
# The twenty-two below are precisely the ones "fluid_styled_content" declares
# in its own "Configuration/TypoScript/setup.typoscript" at v14.3.7.
#
# On v13.4 that extension declares twenty-THREE: it still ships
# "ContentElement/List.typoscript", which this file does not clear. That is
# deliberate and safe, and it was read rather than assumed - v13's
# "List.typoscript" is "tt_content.list =< lib.contentElement" plus
# "templateName = List" and nothing else, and the re-import at the bottom of
# this file declares "tt_content.list" with "templateName = Generic", which
# overwrites it. Nothing of that branch survives, so clearing it would buy
# nothing and would cost the plugin registrations described below.
#
# They are not all equally load bearing, and the difference was measured rather
# than assumed. "header", "text", "div" and "html" get nothing from that
# extension but a "templateName", which this theme overwrites when it declares
# its own - removing their ">" lines changes no rendered byte, and they are kept
# as a defence against that extension gaining data processing for them later.
# The branches that genuinely leak are the ones carrying a "dataProcessing" or
# "variables" block: the galleries, "bullets", "table", "uploads", "shortcut"
# and the menus. "menu_categorized_content" is the sharpest of them - both
# extensions wire "DatabaseQueryProcessor" there and the merged keys compose one
# query out of two, which fails as a SQL syntax error rather than as wrong
# markup.
#
# "tt_content.list" is deliberately NOT cleared. It is the historical plugin
# CType, and on TYPO3 v13 "ExtensionUtility::configurePlugin()" writes straight
# into it - "tt_content.list.20.<signature> = EXTBASEPLUGIN" - through
# "defaultContentRendering", which the two delivery paths add at a point this
# file cannot see. Clearing it could drop a third-party plugin's own
# registration, which is a far worse failure than the leftover it would
# prevent, and on v14 the CType does not exist at all.

tt_content.header >
tt_content.text >
tt_content.image >
tt_content.textpic >
tt_content.textmedia >
tt_content.bullets >
tt_content.table >
tt_content.uploads >
tt_content.div >
tt_content.html >
tt_content.shortcut >
tt_content.menu_pages >
tt_content.menu_subpages >
tt_content.menu_section >
tt_content.menu_section_pages >
tt_content.menu_sitemap >
tt_content.menu_sitemap_pages >
tt_content.menu_abstract >
tt_content.menu_recently_updated >
tt_content.menu_related_pages >
tt_content.menu_categorized_pages >
tt_content.menu_categorized_content >

# The theme's own rendering, declared again on the cleared branches. This is
# the very file the theme's own setup imports, so there is one definition of
# the classic elements and not a second copy to keep in step.
#
# It re-declares "lib.contentElement = FLUIDTEMPLATE" as a plain assignment,
# which keeps every child "fluid_styled_content" put there - its templates at
# index "0", the integrator's "{$styles.templates.*}" at "10", its "settings",
# and on v14 its "dataProcessing.1770716912 = record-transformation" - and adds
# the theme's own paths at "5", between the two. See the comment on that object
# for why "5".
#
# That data processor is the one leftover this file keeps on purpose. It runs on
# every classic element in the bridged configuration and on none of them
# standalone, and it is harmless where the others are not:
# "RecordTransformationProcessor" writes a "record" variable *beside* "data"
# rather than replacing it, and no template of this theme reads "record". That
# is why the bridged page still compares byte for byte against the standalone
# one even though this processor ran.
@import 'EXT:theme_extension_development/Configuration/TypoScript/ContentElements.typoscript'
